## EU in-region routing

- [OpenRouter EU](https://openrouter.ai/business/eu): EU in-region routing on OpenRouter Business. Requests sent to https://eu.openrouter.ai are decrypted in the EU and routed only to shared provider endpoints located in Europe (the EU/EEA, the UK, and Switzerland); prompts and completions are processed there, while account data, billing records, authentication data, security logs, and other operational records may be stored and processed in the US. Requests served by a customer's BYOK key go to the customer's own cloud deployment: the customer provisions it in the region they need and sets the key's region per provider, and OpenRouter does not verify where it runs. Self-serve on Business: no contract, no monthly minimum. Lists the live EU model catalog, the data boundary, and data-region guardrail setup.
- [EU Model API](https://eu.openrouter.ai/api/v1/models): Machine-readable list of models with endpoints in Europe (the EU/EEA, the UK, and Switzerland), with EU endpoint pricing. Batch (:batch) variants appear in this list but are not accepted on regional domains; the Batch API runs only on openrouter.ai.
- [In-region routing docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/features/in-region-routing): Regional base URLs, fail-closed behavior, and the features regional domains reject.

## Ori

- [Ori](https://openrouter.ai/ori): OpenRouter's family of tools for putting agents to work with any model: Ori Harness, Ori Code, Ori Eval, Ori Intern, and Ori Desktop.
- [Ori Harness](https://openrouter.ai/ori/harness): Run the agent CLI you already use — Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Hermes, and more — on OpenRouter, with OAuth sign-in and your org's guardrails.
- [Ori Eval](https://openrouter.ai/ori/eval.md): Find the best model for your project — run your agent on your own prompts, on a harness and model that stay pinned, and rank the candidates.
- [spawn-ori-eval skill](https://openrouter.ai/skills/spawn-ori-eval): For coding agents. Read it to run a model eval by handing it to Ori, so the eval is authored and graded on a pinned harness and model rather than one you improvised.
- [install-ori-harness skill](https://openrouter.ai/skills/install-ori-harness): For coding agents. Read it to install Ori, sign in, run an existing agent CLI through Ori, choose an OpenRouter model, and verify the setup.
- [Install Ori](https://openrouter.ai/labs/ori/install.sh): `curl -fsSL https://openrouter.ai/labs/ori/install.sh | bash`
- [Ori Eval docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/ori/eval.md): Writing `*.eval.ts` files, LLM-as-judge grading, and model bakeoffs.
- [Ori Harness docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/ori/harness.md): Installing Ori, signing in, and running each supported agent CLI on OpenRouter.

